	Very Artistic was an R&B trio signed to Dreamworks/Universal around 2000. Their only album, the 15 track One by One (2001), was shelved and only advance copies exist. The album was produced and executive produced by production duo Tim & Bob and production collective The Characters (primarly Troy Taylor and Charles Farrar). The track "We Make Love" was co-produced by  LaMont Fleming. The group is very obscure, as they did not even release a single. The album's cancellation is largely attributed to a massive shift in executive priorities at DreamWorks Records right before its commercial music division was entirely dissolved and sold to Universal Music Group. Critics felt the album ultimately suffered from overbearing production and typical 2000s R&B clichés, leading some to joke that V.A. stood for "Very Average".

